# Sibling projects and scratch trees kept in this working copy but not part of
# this repository.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is load-bearing
# rather than tidiness. An unanchored pattern matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, and `docs` in particular was matching `frontend/src/app/docs/`
# — the app's own documentation ROUTES. Two consequences, both silent:
#
#   1. Those pages were never tracked by git. `git status` did not list them,
#      `git ls-files` returned nothing for them, and a fresh clone would have
#      been missing the whole /docs section of the site.
#   2. Tailwind's source scanner respects .gitignore, so it skipped the
#      directory and never generated the utilities used only in there — the
#      docs sidebar's `hidden md:block` and `md:grid-cols-[13.75rem_1fr]` were
#      absent from the stylesheet, so the sidebar was invisible at every width.
#
# `command grep`/ugrep in this shell also honours these patterns, which is why
# a recursive search for a string in those files reported zero hits.
#
# Keep the leading slash on anything added here.
/copypools
/subgraphs
/pitch
/docs
/tickwise

node_modules

.DS_Store
